{"type": "decision.logged", "title": "Turn the event log into a control mechanism (loop & graph engineering)", "rationale": "AIPIM was a system of record with its process living in CLAUDE.md prose that no code enforced, and a dependency graph that existed in the type system but was dropped by applyEvent. Three changes make the event log a control mechanism: a verification gate over check.run evidence events that blocks complete_task without a fresh passing run; task dependencies promoted to read-model state so get_next_task returns only the ready frontier; and Claude Code hooks that execute the session protocol instead of asking the model to remember it.", "filePath": ".project/decisions/2026-08-12-ADR010-loop-and-graph-engineering.md", "id": "1786545477101-adr1", "timestamp": "2026-08-12T12:01:00.000Z", "actor": "rmarsigli@gmail.com"}
